WEBVTT

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:03.530
Everyone, Kaleido Star is about to start!

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:06.480
When watching Kaleido Star,
please keep the room brightly lit,

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.040
and sit as far from the TV as you can.

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:14.350
I'm Sora Naegino.
I came to America all by myself

00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:15.950
with aspirations of joining Kaleido Stage.

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:17.690
Everything is new to me,

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:20.880
but I'm doing my best in the spirit of
"try it rather than think about it."

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:22.590
There's nothing I can't do if I try

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:24.360
and if I can do it without trying,
I'd be super lucky.

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.350
And if I'm gonna do it, I just gotta do it!
Gotta! Gotta! That's me.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:33.160
Well, well, well, everyone,
do you have a pet at home?

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:36.440
A pet that you feed and take on walks.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.040
They can be quite troublesome.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.010
But still, they're adorable, aren't they?

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:41.570
After all, they're a member of the family.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.850
No matter how much he's against it,

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:46.970
I'm not gonna give up this time either!
Not gonna! Not gonna!

00:01:02.630 --> 00:01:05.760
<i>Yaritai koto wa nani</i>

00:01:02.630 --> 00:01:05.760
<i>What is it that you want to do?</i>

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:09.400
<i>Sou kikareru tabi</i>

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:09.400
<i>Every time I was asked that</i>

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:13.130
<i>Aoi sora miageta</i>

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:13.130
<i>I looked up at the blue sky</i>

00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:17.150
<i>Kotae wa only my heart</i>

00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:17.150
<i>The answer is only in my heart</i>

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:24.650
<i>Honto ni daiji na kotoba wa
kantan ni wa iwanai</i>

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:24.650
<i>I don't easily say the words
that are really important</i>

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:31.960
<i>Hikari ga yubisasu basho e to hashiridasu yo</i>

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:31.960
<i>I start running towards the place
the light points to</i>

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:39.940
<i>Dakishimetai mono nara
nakitai hodo mune ni aru</i>

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:39.940
<i>There's so much in my heart that I want
to embrace, I could cry</i>

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:46.880
<i>Egakitsuzukete yuku kitto
take it someday</i>

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:46.880
<i>I'll keep painting my way, I promise,
take it someday</i>

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:54.850
<i>Shiroi kumo ga nagareru
chiheisen no mukou ni</i>

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:54.850
<i>Beyond the horizon,
where the white clouds drift</i>

00:01:54.850 --> 00:02:06.630
<i>Naranderu mirai wa itsumo soba ni aru kara</i>

00:01:54.850 --> 00:02:06.630
<i>The future is lined up and
it'll always be there by my side</i>

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:25.480
Kaleido Stage's Cinderella is a must-see.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:28.550
In the show, the performance of
a trio of new-comers

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:31.880
as the fairy godmothers was fascinating
during the climactic scene.

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:35.110
We will be watching these girls in the future.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:37.320
We will be watching!

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.890
Yes, watch us!

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:43.600
The paper's praising us!

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:44.630
We did it!

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:47.170
We did it! We did it! We did it!
We did it! We did it!

00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:49.760
Wow! I'm so happy!

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:56.330
What's this?

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:03.410
This is... a baby seal?

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:10.190
The Amazing Seal

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:10.190
"The Amazing Seal"

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:13.090
The Amazing Seal

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:19.840
He must have gotten separated
from his parents.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.100
Poor baby.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.720
Well, I'll be gone for just a bit.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.020
Please take care of him, Fool.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.790
What?! Take care of him?

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:46.360
What am I suppose to do?

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:48.260
For the time being,

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:49.920
I shall try reading your fortune!

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.930
The upright Hanged Man.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:02.440
This card represents ordeals or sacrifices.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:06.070
It may bring misfortune.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:07.550
Yes?

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:10.920
Oh, can you see me?!

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:14.190
You are wrong if you think
you can be a Kaleido Star

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:15.990
just because you can see me!

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:19.150
Good morning, Sora.

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:20.330
Sora?

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:22.190
I'm hungry.

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.400
I wonder if she left for the
dining hall already?

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:38.910
A misfortune is befalling me.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:44.890
What's with this paper?

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:46.350
They're praising the fairy godmothers.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:47.860
They have no eye for talent.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:50.830
It's like, if I were doing it,
they would've praised us more.

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:53.730
Hey, you'll hurt her feelings if she hears you.

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:55.700
Oh, that would be like, awful.

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:56.930
I should be careful.

00:04:57.570 --> 00:04:59.840
Oh, you're right here. Sorry.

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:01.100
Sorry.

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:04.200
Let's see...

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:06.170
Good morning.

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:07.800
Oh, good morning, Ken.

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:10.380
Something bothering you?

00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:14.080
I was just wondering what he would like.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.520
He?

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:19.550
Yeah. I met him this morning when
I was jogging on the beach.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:24.820
He's cute, round, chubby, small,
and he's very hungry.

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:27.830
What type of guy do you like?

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:28.660
Guy?

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:31.000
I'm not talking about any guy. He's a seal.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:34.140
Se... Seal?

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:35.000
Yes.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:37.370
Please don't tell me you brought him home.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:38.860
Well...

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:40.210
You brought him?

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:43.300
But he was hungry and I felt sorry for him.

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:47.070
So I'm not allowed to keep him?

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:48.020
Come with me.

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:49.210
Oh, okay.

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:54.020
But, he's still small and
he's probably just a baby.

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:56.320
He was weak, and he looked like
he could die at any moment.

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:58.880
So I wanted to do something for him.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:03.530
Seals eat fresh fish.

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:05.890
Thank you.

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:08.970
You have to return him to the sea
once he recovers, all right?

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:11.230
Okay.

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:13.410
Huh? It's open.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:15.280
Thanks for waiting.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:16.840
It's time for your meal.

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:19.710
What are you doing, Fool?

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:24.020
I can't believe this! He's not here!

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:25.010
I'm in trouble!

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:28.580
Rather, it is I who is in trouble.

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:35.200
No, he's not there.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:36.870
Maybe he went back to the sea.

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:37.770
No way!

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:39.430
Are you looking for him?

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:42.930
So he's your friend.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:45.970
Oh, Jonathan!

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:50.270
What?! Who's Jonathan?

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:53.050
It scared me.

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:56.020
This little guy was scooting down
the hallway.

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:01.320
He was dragging this.

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:03.620
Sorry about that.

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:07.520
Isn't he adorable?

00:07:07.930 --> 00:07:11.400
Is there any way for me to keep him?

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:12.370
What?!

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:13.500
Keep him?!

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:15.970
Didn't you just promise to
let him go after feeding him?

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:21.800
I think Jonathan could be a mascot
for Kaleido Stage.

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:23.930
Right, Jonathan?

00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:28.480
Oh, I'm in trouble!

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:30.250
I've got lessons to go to!

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:32.390
Would you please look after him
for a little while?!

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:33.360
What?!

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:34.380
Hey!

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:37.660
She does everything in her own way.

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:39.920
Well, that's what's so great about her too.

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:44.760
Good morning!

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:46.200
Good morning!

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:47.740
Did you read it? Did you read it?

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:48.840
I did! I did! I did!

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:49.800
The paper!

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:52.740
You there! Quiet down!

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:53.710
Yes, sir.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:56.640
This is a message from Kalos.

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:58.950
Although the paper praised
your performance,

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:01.980
the Triple Illusion is far from perfect.

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:04.580
Do not get carried away and lose your focus.

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:06.320
That's all.

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:08.050
Why can't he say that to us himself?

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:10.560
I heard that Kalos will be
in Seattle for a week

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:12.260
to attend a new production meeting.

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:13.730
A new production?

00:08:13.730 --> 00:08:17.230
It seems to be the meeting for the
next production after Cinderella.

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:19.930
Big projects like these
take time to prepare for.

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:22.070
Really? I didn't know that.

00:08:22.070 --> 00:08:24.940
So basically, we'll be fine as long
as we don't make mistakes.

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:25.940
Right.

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:29.180
Let's practice hard for our Triple Illusion.

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:30.080
Yeah.

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:32.210
All right, just you watch, Kalos!

00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:33.780
I'll make you burst out laughing!

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:34.940
That's not it.

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:40.610
What's this? What the hell is this?!

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:46.050
Jonathan!

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:47.360
Who?!

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:50.700
Um, I found him at the beach.

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:52.620
I'm sorry for scaring you.

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:55.360
What are you thinking?

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:59.470
Well, he was hungry and
I felt sorry for him, so...

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:01.980
You can barely perform your own duties.

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:04.500
There is no way you can look after an animal.

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:06.350
But...

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:07.940
Take him back right now!

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:20.900
Sorry,

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:22.590
I took my eyes off him for just a second.

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:25.500
No, it's okay.

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:28.540
I asked some veteran staff members,

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:31.940
but they said that Kaleido Stage
has never had any animals.

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:34.530
That seems to be Kalos' policy.

00:09:35.140 --> 00:09:37.630
Maybe it's a good thing this happened
while Kalos was away.

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:39.810
You can't keep him, Sora.

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:43.350
But he's still just a baby.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:45.950
I don't think he can't survive by himself.

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:48.950
He's small, but he'll eat quite a lot of food.

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:51.520
The cost of feeding him won't be cheap.

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:54.500
I'm getting a performer's pay now.

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:56.700
And I'm going to start a
part-time job tomorrow.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:57.760
What?!

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:59.070
Part-time job?

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:01.670
You have lessons during the day
and performances in the evening!

00:10:01.670 --> 00:10:04.970
Sora, now is the most important time for us.

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:07.210
I know.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:08.700
I know that, but...

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:15.020
After my parents died, I was all alone.

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:21.820
If no one had opened their arms,

00:10:25.460 --> 00:10:29.120
I'm sure I wouldn't be here right now.

00:10:32.470 --> 00:10:34.660
That's why I can't abandon him.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:37.740
You can call me a hypocrite,

00:10:38.210 --> 00:10:39.470
but I just can't abandon him.

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:43.550
Don't worry,

00:10:43.550 --> 00:10:45.840
I'll work harder than ever on my performance.

00:10:57.230 --> 00:10:58.760
Thank you for letting me use your bath.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:01.660
You're welcome. But are you really okay?

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:03.390
Yup. Good night.

00:11:03.770 --> 00:11:04.750
Good night.

00:11:08.970 --> 00:11:10.100
I'm home.

00:11:12.340 --> 00:11:13.860
How do you like it, Jonathan?

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:20.780
I'm sorry to keep you
in such a cramped place.

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:22.850
The inside of the drawer is also cramped.

00:11:22.850 --> 00:11:24.890
When I have time off, let's go to the beach.

00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:26.050
The beach!

00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:27.720
Wearing a bathing suit is the best way
for us to get to know each other.

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:29.420
Just the two of us, Jonathan!

00:11:30.390 --> 00:11:32.190
She treats me worse than animals.

00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:02.220
All right.

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:03.930
That is all for today's lesson.

00:12:03.930 --> 00:12:05.090
Thank you.

00:12:03.930 --> 00:12:05.090
That is all for today's lesson.

00:12:05.090 --> 00:12:05.630
Thank you.

00:12:05.630 --> 00:12:06.720
Sora!

00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:08.360
What?!

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:09.460
There she goes.

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:14.770
Thank you for waiting.

00:12:14.770 --> 00:12:16.470
Here's your Pirate Pizza.

00:12:16.470 --> 00:12:19.470
Two orders of Chef's Special,

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:21.240
Bolognese linguine.

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:21.980
The main entrees are sea bass and lobster.

00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:24.210
Signorina, here's today's pay.

00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:24.210
The main entrees are sea bass and lobster.

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:26.150
Yes, thank you!

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:31.620
But are you really sure you want
fresh fish instead of money everyday?

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:34.450
Yes, he eats a lot of fish, so this will help.

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:36.790
Well, I have to go now.

00:12:39.430 --> 00:12:41.450
He must really love fish.

00:12:41.730 --> 00:12:42.990
Here!

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:46.230
That's all.

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:51.570
You still want more?!

00:12:56.310 --> 00:12:57.040
Yeah!

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:58.110
Yeah!

00:12:58.610 --> 00:12:59.310
Yeah!

00:12:59.850 --> 00:13:00.720
Job well done.

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:01.700
Thanks.

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:05.580
Wasn't our timing for the cross jump
just perfect today?

00:13:06.150 --> 00:13:08.920
Yeah, I wish Kalos could have seen it.

00:13:09.990 --> 00:13:12.290
Kalos just had to be gone
when we did it right.

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:16.660
Anyway, Sora, are you going to work
after this again today?

00:13:16.660 --> 00:13:17.630
Yeah.

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:20.070
You've been working non-stop
for a whole week, right?

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:22.070
You shouldn't push yourself too much.

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:23.660
Don't worry, don't worry.

00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:27.240
You broke one again?!

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.540
Break another one and you're fired.

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:31.440
I'm sorry.

00:13:33.180 --> 00:13:35.840
I have the day off tomorrow,
no performance or lessons.

00:13:36.450 --> 00:13:37.920
Just hang in there a little longer.

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:47.560
I'm home.

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:51.030
What was that?!

00:13:53.900 --> 00:13:55.130
Sora?!

00:14:02.310 --> 00:14:04.350
Well, I just missed dinner.

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:06.380
So I ran out of energy and I got dizzy.

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:07.820
That's not "dizzy"!

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:08.420
Okay!

00:14:08.420 --> 00:14:08.880
Here.

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:09.180
That's why I told you not to
push yourself too much!

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:09.180
Here.

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:10.820
That's why I told you not to
push yourself too much!

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:11.890
Sorry.

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:11.990
Lessons  -  Fliers  -  Lessons  -  Building Cleaning
Newspaper  -  Stage  -  Sleep  -  Restaurant

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:13.490
Lessons  -  Fliers  -  Lessons  -  Building Cleaning
Newspaper  -  Stage  -  Sleep  -  Restaurant

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:13.490
What's this?!

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:15.620
Lessons  -  Fliers  -  Lessons  -  Building Cleaning
Newspaper  -  Stage  -  Sleep  -  Restaurant

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:15.620
You were working this many jobs?!

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:18.220
No wonder you collapsed.

00:14:19.730 --> 00:14:23.130
But Jonathan eats so much.

00:14:23.430 --> 00:14:25.160
And he gets hungry really fast.

00:14:25.270 --> 00:14:27.560
Look, that's it.

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:31.410
Anyway, this has to go!

00:14:31.410 --> 00:14:32.240
What?!

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:34.940
You won't give up even if
we tried to stop you.

00:14:35.340 --> 00:14:36.910
So we have no choice but to help you.

00:14:36.910 --> 00:14:38.000
Hold on.

00:14:38.450 --> 00:14:41.750
I think it can be done if we take turns.

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:42.520
Yeah, I agree.

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:46.150
No, this is Jonathan and my problem, so...

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:48.750
This is our problem too!

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:50.460
Mia...

00:14:50.460 --> 00:14:51.260
Isn't that right?

00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:52.920
Oh, I just remember something!

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:56.230
Juggling contest?

00:14:56.230 --> 00:14:57.230
That's right.

00:14:57.230 --> 00:15:00.740
This is an annual event held on the
outdoor stage at the beach.

00:15:00.740 --> 00:15:04.510
All the jugglers who are confident
in their skill participate in the contest.

00:15:04.510 --> 00:15:06.470
The contest is...

00:15:06.470 --> 00:15:07.310
three days from now.

00:15:07.310 --> 00:15:08.710
People who want to participate

00:15:08.710 --> 00:15:11.440
must register by 9 AM
on the day of the contest.

00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:13.250
Can anyone participate?

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:14.210
Yes.

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:15.550
Wow!

00:15:15.550 --> 00:15:16.620
What?

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:19.750
The first prize could pay for a
whole month of food for Jonathan.

00:15:21.090 --> 00:15:23.280
Then we have no choice but to participate!

00:15:25.490 --> 00:15:27.860
Oh... But l...

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:29.300
What's wrong?

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:30.670
Are you worried about something?

00:15:30.670 --> 00:15:33.860
I've never juggled.

00:15:35.440 --> 00:15:37.070
It could still be okay.

00:15:37.070 --> 00:15:39.440
That's right, we have three days.

00:15:39.440 --> 00:15:40.010
Really?

00:15:40.010 --> 00:15:42.210
Yup, yup, yup, yup, yup, yup.

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:43.410
You think so?

00:15:43.410 --> 00:15:44.580
That's right!

00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:45.880
The level of competition is high,

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:47.620
but as they say, "You've nothing to lose."

00:15:47.620 --> 00:15:47.820
Miss Sarah!

00:15:47.620 --> 00:15:47.820
but as they say, "You've nothing to lose."

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:48.280
Miss Sarah!

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:50.890
Oops... Sorry.

00:15:50.890 --> 00:15:52.090
Let's start a crash course!

00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:53.080
Yeah!

00:16:00.530 --> 00:16:01.500
What?!

00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:03.490
The upright Wheel of Fortune.

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:05.660
A messenger for good fortune?

00:16:06.100 --> 00:16:08.300
Him? Impossible!

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:16.980
Sora! I have great news!

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:19.250
If you win the juggling contest,

00:16:19.250 --> 00:16:21.410
a month's worth of food for Jonathan...

00:16:23.890 --> 00:16:25.050
Look, look. Here, here!

00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:27.860
Oh, so she already knew.

00:16:27.860 --> 00:16:29.250
A little more.

00:16:31.230 --> 00:16:32.190
Yes.

00:16:32.990 --> 00:16:34.030
Not like that.

00:16:34.030 --> 00:16:34.560
Oh, no.

00:16:34.560 --> 00:16:35.660
Do it more rhythmical like this.

00:16:35.660 --> 00:16:37.530
Okay, okay.

00:16:37.670 --> 00:16:39.570
No, I can't do it!

00:16:39.570 --> 00:16:40.670
Do it faster!

00:16:40.670 --> 00:16:43.640
Oh! If I can't even do something like this,

00:16:44.340 --> 00:16:46.810
I can't expect to become a Kaleido Star.

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:50.940
I didn't think you were that bad.

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:55.380
Did you know there was a cast member
who tried to keep a dog

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:57.180
and got fired by Kalos for it?

00:16:57.180 --> 00:16:58.150
What?!

00:16:58.420 --> 00:17:02.250
My dad said that Kalos is
coming back on Monday.

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:06.560
Wow!

00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:12.270
Jonathan, you're better than Sora!

00:17:12.270 --> 00:17:14.030
Jonathan, you're good! Very good!

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:15.800
Great! You're great!

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:20.770
Oh...

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:24.070
Hey, Jonathan, do it one more time.

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:25.840
One more time.

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:29.180
It looks like he won't do it
unless he feels like it.

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:31.620
He acts just like a big star.

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:32.690
Not too bad.

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:35.350
If Jonathan can do it, I should be able to...

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:39.730
All right.

00:17:39.730 --> 00:17:41.530
In that case,

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:42.960
let's go for the crowd pleaser.

00:17:45.970 --> 00:17:49.870
Now, the juggling contest
is getting more exciting!

00:17:49.870 --> 00:17:54.930
Next up are regulars you already know,
Mr. and Mrs. Pumpkin!

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:05.150
Ooh, they're veteran performers for you.

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:06.050
Wow! They're the best.

00:18:06.050 --> 00:18:07.660
They're pretty good.

00:18:06.050 --> 00:18:07.660
Wow! They're the best.

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:10.090
It could be difficult for Sora's team to win.

00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:16.630
It's me.

00:18:17.260 --> 00:18:19.490
Yeah. I got back a day early.

00:18:21.670 --> 00:18:22.640
Sora is?

00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:33.480
This costume is tight.

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:35.350
That's because it's a rental.

00:18:35.350 --> 00:18:37.690
Don't miss the timing to
bring out the balls, Sora.

00:18:37.690 --> 00:18:38.450
I know.

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:41.290
Once Mia and Anna finish juggling... Okay.

00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:42.220
Well, next up are three very attractive sisters,

00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:42.220
Once Mia and Anna finish juggling... Okay.

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:42.890
Well, next up are three very attractive sisters,

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:44.960
Well, next up are three very attractive sisters,

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:44.960
Anna, that's a bit too much.

00:18:44.960 --> 00:18:45.460
the Jonathan Sisters! Here they are!

00:18:44.960 --> 00:18:45.460
Anna, that's a bit too much.

00:18:45.460 --> 00:18:46.430
the Jonathan Sisters! Here they are!

00:18:45.460 --> 00:18:46.430
Really?

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:47.190
the Jonathan Sisters! Here they are!

00:18:47.190 --> 00:18:48.660
It's our turn!

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:50.860
Finally, it's Sora's group.

00:18:51.270 --> 00:18:52.760
We need them to do their best.

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:03.080
Sora!

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:04.150
She blew it.

00:19:04.150 --> 00:19:05.480
Shoot!

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:07.280
Oh, no!

00:19:10.350 --> 00:19:11.350
Hey, hey.

00:19:11.350 --> 00:19:12.320
Jonathan?

00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:13.450
Jonathan!

00:19:16.190 --> 00:19:17.250
Jonathan!

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:26.530
We were saved by Jonathan.

00:19:26.530 --> 00:19:27.590
Anna!

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:35.840
Bravo, Jonathan!

00:19:42.980 --> 00:19:43.950
Kalos...

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:46.720
Isn't he supposed to come back tomorrow?

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:48.880
What should we do?

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:52.050
I'll go.

00:19:53.460 --> 00:19:55.400
I cannot allow you to work part-time.

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:57.090
Nor can I allow pets.

00:19:57.700 --> 00:19:59.670
Keep your attention focused on
performing on stage.

00:19:59.670 --> 00:20:00.330
That's all.

00:20:00.330 --> 00:20:01.570
You can go now.

00:20:01.570 --> 00:20:03.370
I'm not losing my focus.

00:20:03.370 --> 00:20:05.510
In fact, when you were away, we
did a perfect...

00:20:05.510 --> 00:20:07.100
This discussion is over.

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:10.200
I'm not going to abandon Jonathan.

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:12.410
Who?

00:20:12.410 --> 00:20:13.980
If I abandon him,

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:15.750
Jonathan will die.

00:20:15.750 --> 00:20:19.050
If you cannot abandon him,
then you should quit Kaleido Stage.

00:20:19.050 --> 00:20:20.120
No, I won't!

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:21.090
What?!

00:20:23.890 --> 00:20:24.590
What is it?

00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:26.080
Boss, you have a guest.

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:27.960
Okay. I'll be there soon.

00:20:28.300 --> 00:20:29.800
I told you the discussion is over.

00:20:29.800 --> 00:20:30.700
Not yet.

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:31.960
That's enough!

00:20:32.300 --> 00:20:35.040
I think the show has nothing to do
with Jonathan.

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:35.800
It does!

00:20:35.800 --> 00:20:38.070
Listen, get rid of him!

00:20:38.070 --> 00:20:40.640
If you have time for something like that,
you should practice more!

00:20:40.640 --> 00:20:41.610
Understand?

00:20:41.610 --> 00:20:42.840
Of course, I will.

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:45.610
I will work harder than ever for the stage,

00:20:45.610 --> 00:20:47.710
so that all the papers will come to see us.

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:51.190
I think Kaleido Stage exists

00:20:51.190 --> 00:20:54.920
to make people happy when
they come see us.

00:20:55.560 --> 00:21:00.050
But abandoning Jonathan
in exchange for that...

00:21:00.430 --> 00:21:02.690
I think there's something wrong with that.

00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:05.200
Although I can't say what exactly,

00:21:05.630 --> 00:21:09.730
I still think there's something
wrong with that.

00:21:16.180 --> 00:21:17.200
Kalos.

00:21:18.410 --> 00:21:19.380
Jean.

00:21:20.110 --> 00:21:22.420
Jonathan... Everybody...

00:21:22.420 --> 00:21:27.120
Kalos, now I understand why you let
Sora join Kaleido Stage.

00:21:27.990 --> 00:21:29.820
It was my biggest mistake.

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:31.890
How about it?

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:34.990
Why don't we take care of the seal here?

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:39.070
That way, Sora can quit her part-time jobs

00:21:39.600 --> 00:21:42.430
and there won't be any worries on
how it will affect her performance.

00:21:45.470 --> 00:21:47.740
I'll let you handle this, Jean.

00:21:49.080 --> 00:21:52.240
Let's build a gigantic swimming pool
for Jonathan.

00:21:52.750 --> 00:21:53.840
Dad!

00:21:56.420 --> 00:21:58.750
Sora, Kalos gave you permission!

00:21:58.750 --> 00:21:59.810
Did you hear?!

00:22:03.860 --> 00:22:05.660
Thank you so much!

00:22:07.630 --> 00:22:09.030
All right!

00:22:09.030 --> 00:22:10.890
Isn't this great, Jonathan?

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:24.550
<i>When you sabishii toki doushitemasuka</i>

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:24.550
<i>When you're lonely, what do you do?</i>

00:22:24.550 --> 00:22:26.980
<i>Never say sonna no wakannai</i>

00:22:24.550 --> 00:22:26.980
<i>Never say you don't get any of that</i>

00:22:26.980 --> 00:22:29.850
<i>Nemuru asobu magazine mekuru</i>

00:22:26.980 --> 00:22:29.850
<i>Sleep, play, flip through a magazine</i>

00:22:29.850 --> 00:22:32.190
<i>Sabishii toki wa sabishii yo</i>

00:22:29.850 --> 00:22:32.190
<i>When you're lonely, you're lonely</i>

00:22:32.190 --> 00:22:36.990
<i>Mienai denpa ga kyou mo
tulututu machi ni tobikau</i>

00:22:32.190 --> 00:22:36.990
<i>Like always, invisible vibes fly around
the city today, tulututu</i>

00:22:36.990 --> 00:22:41.630
<i>Anyway kokoro no bekutoru
so many reason hanashiteru</i>

00:22:36.990 --> 00:22:41.630
<i>Anyway, the vector of my heart is
talking about so many reasons</i>

00:22:41.630 --> 00:22:46.330
<i>Jiyuu ni sora o tobitai keredo</i>

00:22:41.630 --> 00:22:46.330
<i>I want to be free and fly the skies</i>

00:22:46.330 --> 00:22:51.010
<i>Hane o hirogeru basho ga nai</i>

00:22:46.330 --> 00:22:51.010
<i>But I don't have space to spread my wings</i>

00:22:51.010 --> 00:22:53.210
<i>Demo shinjiteru</i>

00:22:51.010 --> 00:22:53.210
<i>But I have faith</i>

00:22:53.210 --> 00:22:57.850
<i>Katachi no nai mirai ga aru yo</i>

00:22:53.210 --> 00:22:57.850
<i>There is a future yet to be shaped</i>

00:22:57.850 --> 00:23:02.550
<i>Katachi ni shitai watashi ga iru</i>

00:22:57.850 --> 00:23:02.550
<i>And there's a me that I want to shape</i>

00:23:02.550 --> 00:23:09.020
<i>Kanashikutemo machigai demo</i>

00:23:02.550 --> 00:23:09.020
<i>Even if I'm sad, even if it's a mistake</i>

00:23:09.020 --> 00:23:14.360
<i>Omou mama fly to the free</i>

00:23:09.020 --> 00:23:14.360
<i>I'll do what I want and
fly towards the freedom</i>

00:23:20.300 --> 00:23:22.170
Next Kaleido Star

00:23:22.740 --> 00:23:24.510
They don't appreciate my performance

00:23:24.510 --> 00:23:26.170
because the audience isn't
sophisticated enough!

00:23:26.170 --> 00:23:29.480
And so, a talented diabolo girl,
Rosetta, has come.

00:23:29.480 --> 00:23:30.240
Amazing...

00:23:30.240 --> 00:23:31.780
She is truly the world champion.

00:23:31.780 --> 00:23:33.650
But she looks sad somehow.

00:23:33.650 --> 00:23:36.880
The stage is supposed to make
the audience happy with our smiles.

00:23:36.880 --> 00:23:39.890
That's why I wanna see Rosetta smile
no matter what.

00:23:39.890 --> 00:23:40.950
I wanna! I wanna!

00:23:41.460 --> 00:23:42.920
Next time on Kaleido Star,
"The Amazing Girl Who Doesn't Smile"

00:23:42.920 --> 00:23:45.590
The Amazing Girl Who Doesn't Smile

00:23:42.920 --> 00:23:45.590
Next time on Kaleido Star,
"The Amazing Girl Who Doesn't Smile"

00:23:45.590 --> 00:23:47.960
The Amazing Girl Who Doesn't Smile

